# Documentation toolchain for the embedded `/docs` site: the direct
# requirements. `requirements-docs.txt` is the lock compiled from this file,
# with every transitive package pinned and hashed, and it is what gets installed.
#
# The site is built with `mkdocs build` (output: site/) and embedded into the
# YANuget binary. It must remain fully offline — keep `font: false` in
# mkdocs.yml and do not add plugins that fetch remote assets. Bump this version
# deliberately when updating the bundled theme.
#
# The lock is installed with `pip install --require-hashes`: in CI, in the
# release builds and in the container image, this code runs next to a token or
# ends up inside a published artifact, and a bare range meant that any new
# upload to PyPI ran there unreviewed. After editing this file, regenerate the
# lock. It is universal so that the Windows and macOS release runners install
# the same hashed set as Linux:
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.10 \
#       requirements-docs.in -o requirements-docs.txt
mkdocs-material>=9.5,<10
